  "identity_evidence": "The original Fraser Point label, Coffin Point to the south and MacFarlane Point to the north identify this western Boularderie coast. Native detail resolves a closed offshore island, separated from the mainland by water/engraving lines, immediately north/northwest of the small mainland hook. The matching modern coastal island is original WACOIS10 feature17044 with80 exterior vertices. Both show a northeast-oriented oval island and the same relation to the adjacent headland; smaller modern coastal rocks are not substituted. Trace the innermost island shoreline, excluding external sea engraving contours and mainland lines. The official Fraser Point record CAMXU identifies the locality only. This island supplies a closed physical feature after the nearly straight Kempt western shoreline was withheld.",
